<title>USA: Georgia Power sees Hatch 1 restart Sun-Mon.</title>
<headline>Georgia Power sees Hatch 1 restart Sun-Mon.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-01-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Georgia Power Co said Wednesday it expects its Hatch 1 nuclear power station to restart on Sunday or Monday.</p>
<p>It was taken off line early Wednesday and power reduced to just 10 percent of its rated 741 megawatt (MW) capacity.</p>
<p>&quot;We took it off line at 0130 (EST) this morning. There is a very small leak in a three-quarter inch line inside the drywell buyilding that houses the reactor...We expect it to restart on Sunday or Monday,&quot; said Loretto Stevens, a Georgia Power spokeswoman.</p>
<p>The Hatch nuclear facility is in Baxley, Ga.</p>
<p>Georgia Power Co is a subsidiary of Southern Co.</p>
<p>((--New York Power Desk + 212 859 1628))</p>
